  "note": "The rules a share link is checked by, on the web and in the apps (ADR 0120 decision 4, ADR 0150 decision 2, ADR 0155 decision 7.2): the core's `sharing/` (`ReceivedLink`, `LinkDays`, `ShareInstance`) and `session/ClientWindow` answer every case, and the web draws them through `@veyq/core-js/sharing`; the core's `ShareLinkVectorsTest`, the package's `sharing.test.ts` and the web's tests read this file. `parse`: an accepted input with its normalized `link`, `origin`, `shareId` and `host`, and `report` where its fragment asks the share page to open its report dialog; a refused one with its `problem`, and `moderation` where it is a moderator's review (`#moderation`), which the app refuses with a problem of its own while the bookmark's parse calls it `noKey`. `kept`: a stored link read back — only the normalized form itself reads (`link`), anything else is null. `report`: whether a share page's fragment asks for its report dialog (`asks`), and the fragment it keeps once read (`without`). `lastDay`: the last local day (in `zone`) a link made at `madeAt` may end on under `maxDays` — a picked day is sent as its end, which must not pass `madeAt + maxDays × 24 h`, so an edited link counts from when it was made, never from `now` (when the form opens). `embed`: a share's instance as its `/api/setup` was read (`setup`; null: no answer), the majors this client speaks and this instance's `core.share-embedding` (`embedding`); `app`: whether an app opens the instance's links, `page`: whether a web page shows the share in place (null: yes, else why not). `window`: the older majors ADR 0085 decision 5's planned window keeps for a client of `major`.",
